_1956_V2_AI_HAN_KEYPOINT_CLASS="Hand key point classification",T.Msg._1956_V2_AI_FALL_DEF="Fall detection",T.Msg._1956_V2_AI_OCR_REC="Text recognition",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_DET_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize face detection",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_DET_INIT_TOOLTIP="The face detection application detects each face in the video and marks it with a detection frame. It also identifies the five key points of each face: the left eye, right eye, nose tip, left corner of the mouth, and right corner of the mouth. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_DET_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get face detection result %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize face recognition threshold %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_INIT_TOOLTIP='The face recognition application performs face identity recognition on each frame in the video based on face registration information. If the recognized face is in the registration database, the identity information of the recognized face is annotated; otherwise, the value "unknown" is displayed. ',T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get face recognition result list",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_HAS_MESSAGE0="Face recognition results include %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_GET_RES_NAME_MESSAGE0="Face recognition results obtained: %1, %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REC_GET_HAS_UNKNOWN_FACE_MESSAGE0="There are unrecorded faces",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REG_INIT_MESSAGE0="Enter face, face label %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REG_INIT_TOOLTIP="Face registration is a prerequisite for face recognition. It features each face image in the face database and writes the facial features to the face database directory in the form of a bin file for use by the face recognition program.",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_REG_TRAIN_MESSAGE0="Facial recognition training model",T.Msg._1956_V2_LICENCE_DET_REC_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize license plate recognition",T.Msg._1956_V2_LICENCE_DET_REC_INIT_TOOLTIP="The license plate recognition application is a dual-model task. First, license plates appearing in the video are detected. Then, each detected license plate is recognized and the recognized license plate content is marked near the corresponding detection box. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_LICENCE_DET_REC_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get license plate recognition result list",T.Msg._1956_V2_LICENCE_DET_REC_HAS_MESSAGE0="License plate recognition results include license plate %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_OBJ_REC_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize 80-category object recognition",T.Msg._1956_V2_OBJ_REC_INIT_TOOLTIP="The yolov8n object detection application uses the yolov8n model to detect 80 COCO categories. The detection results are indicated on the screen as detection boxes. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_OBJ_REC_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get 80 object recognition results %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_OBJ_REC_GET_RES_IDS="id list",T.Msg._1956_V2_OBJ_REC_GET_RES_NAMES="name list",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_LANDMARK_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize facial key part detection",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_LANDMARK_INIT_TOOLTIP="The facial key part application is a dual-model application. It first performs face detection on each frame of the video. Then, it identifies 106 key points for each detected face and uses these 106 key points to draw the contours of the face, mouth, eyes, nose, and eyebrows.",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_LANDMARK_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get key facial parts %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_LEFT_EYEBROW="Left eyebrow",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_RIGHT_EYEBROW="Right eyebrow",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_LEFT_EYE="Left eye",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_RIGHT_EYE="Right eye",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_PUPIL="Pupil",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_BRIDGE_NOSE="Bridge of nose",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_WING_NOSE="Wing of nose",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_OUT_LIP="Outer lip",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_IN_LIP="Inner lip",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_BASIN="Face outline",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_PARSE_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initializing face parsing",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_PARSE_INIT_TOOLTIP="The face parsing (also known as face segmentation) application is a dual-model application that first detects faces and then segments them into different parts. Face segmentation involves pixel-level classification of parts like the eyes, nose, and mouth, with different areas indicated by different colors on the screen.",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize face pose",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_INIT_TOOLTIP="Face pose is a dual-model application that first detects faces in each frame of the video and then predicts the face orientation for each detected face. Face orientation is expressed using Euler angles (roll, yaw, and pitch). Roll indicates the degree to which a face is tilted left or right, yaw indicates the degree to which a face is tilted left or right, and pitch indicates the degree to which a face is tilted up or down. This application visualizes the face orientation on the screen by constructing a projection matrix. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get face pose result %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_ORI="Face orientation (raw data)",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_EULER="Face orientation (Euler angles)",T.Msg._1956_V2_FACE_POSE_GET_RES_TOOLTIP="Rotation matrix R (3x3)\nEuler angles [pitch, yaw, roll] (degrees)",T.Msg._1956_V2_PERSON_POINT_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize human key point detection",T.Msg._1956_V2_PERSON_POINT_INIT_TOOLTIP="The human key point detection application uses the yolov8n-pose model to detect human poses. The detection results obtain the positions of 17 human skeleton key points and connect the key points with different colored lines and display them on the screen. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_PERSON_POINT_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get a list of human keypoint coordinates",T.Msg._1956_V2_HAN_KEYPOINT_CLASS_INIT_MESSAGE0="Palm keypoint classification",T.Msg._1956_V2_HAN_KEYPOINT_CLASS_INIT_TOOLTIP="Palm keypoint classification is a dual-model task. First, palms in the video are detected. Then, keypoint regression is performed on the detected palms. After obtaining the keypoint information, the angles between the fingers are calculated to distinguish different gestures. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_HAN_KEYPOINT_CLASS_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Palm keypoint classification result list",T.Msg._1956_V2_HAN_KEYPOINT_CLASS_GET_RES_TYPE_MESSAGE0="Palm keypoint classification: %1 identified",T.Msg._1956_V2_FALL_DEF_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize fall detection",T.Msg._1956_V2_FALL_DEF_INIT_TOOLTIP="The fall detection application checks each frame of the video for the presence of a human and detects the human's fall status. If the human is not falling, it is marked as NoFall; if the human is falling, it is marked as Fall. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_FALL_DEF_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Fall Detection: A fall has been detected.",T.Msg._1956_V2_OCR_REC_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initializing text recognition.",T.Msg._1956_V2_OCR_REC_INIT_TOOLTIP="OCR recognition is a dual-model task. First, text is detected in each frame of the video. Then, the detected text is recognized. Finally, a detection frame is drawn on the screen and the recognized text content is added near the detection frame. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_OCR_REC_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Get text recognition result list",T.Msg._1956_V2_OCR_REC_HAS_MESSAGE0="Text recognition results include %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize self-learning classification %1 Number of classifications %2 Number of training sets for each classification %3",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_TRAIN_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification Start training",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_RECOGNIZE_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification Run recognition",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_INIT_TOOLTIP="Self-learning is a feature-based classification method. First, set labels in the code and set the names of the items to be collected. Then start the application and follow the on-screen prompts to put the items to be collected into the feature collection box. After the feature collection is completed, it will automatically enter the recognition state. Put the items to be recognized into the collection box, and the items will be compared with the registered items in terms of features and classified according to similarity. ",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_GET_RES_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification Get %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_GET_RES_ID="id",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_GET_RES_SCORE="Confidence",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_GET_RES_NAME="Label",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_SET_LABELS_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification Set category label %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_SAVE_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification. Save the trained model to %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_SAVE_TOOLTIP="Self-learning classification. Path is folder",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_LOAD_MESSAGE0="Self-learning classification. Load the self-classification model from %1",T.Msg._1956_V2_SELF_LEARNING_LOAD_TOOLTIP="Path is folder",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_GET_COLOR_MESSAGE0="I2C%1 RGB color %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_GET_ALL_COLOR_MESSAGE0="I2C%1 RGB color",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_GET_COLOR_HSV_MESSAGE0="I2C%1 HSV color %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_GET_ALL_COLOR_HSV_MESSAGE0="I2C%1 HSV color",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_HUM_TEM_MESSAGE0="I2C%1 %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_GESTURE_READGESTURE_MESSAGE0="I2C %1 gesture data",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_ULTRASONIC_MESSAGE0="I2C %1 ultrasonic",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_max30102_INIT_MESSAGE0="I2C %1 heart rate and blood oxygen module initialization",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_SEG_DISPLAY_MESSAGE0="Digital display %1 displays %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_SEG_CLEAR_MESSAGE0="Digital display %1 clears",T.Msg._1956_V2_EncoderMotor_I2C_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initialize encoder motor name %1 pin %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_EncoderMotor_I2C_MESSAGE0="Set encoder motor %1 M1 speed: %2 M2 speed: %3",T.Msg._1956_V2_EncoderMotor_stop_MESSAGE0="Encoder motor %1 stopped",T.Msg._1956_V2_EncoderMotor_angle_MESSAGE0="Set encoder motor %1 %2 speed: %3",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_MP3_INIT_MESSAGE0="Initializing MP3 name %1 pin %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_MP3_1_VOLUME_MESSAGE0="Set MP3 %1 volume to %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_MP3_1_CMD_MESSAGE0="MP3 %1 playing %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_MP3_1_PLAY_SONG_MESSAGE0="MP3 %1 playing song %2",T.Msg._1956_V2_BLUEBIT_MP3_1_